{% comment %}
  Get Outside · Flatirons — paste this whole file into TRMNL's markup editor.

  Variables from the polling endpoint:
    plate_url  time_of_day  weather  message  date_long

  Nesting is fixed by the framework:
    screen -> view view--full -> layout, with title_bar a SIBLING of layout.

  The tile-reveal version of this template is parked at
  flatirons/parked/template-reveal.liquid — see DECISIONS.md #11.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="screen">
  <div class="view view--full">

    <div class="layout">
      <div class="scene">
        {% comment %} No "image-dither" class: the plate is already dithered
        to 8 tones, and dithering it again beats one pattern against another
        and produces moire. {% endcomment %}
        <img class="image scene__plate"
             src="{{ plate_url }}"
             alt="The Boulder Flatirons, {{ time_of_day }}, {{ weather }}" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="title_bar">
      <span class="title">{{ message }}</span>
      <span class="instance">{{ date_long }}</span>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>

<style>
  /* Fill whatever the framework gives us. It sizes the layout itself:
       layout height = screen-h - (gap * 2) - title-bar-height
     which on an 800x480 device is 480 - 20 - 40 = 420, with the art area
     780 wide. Percentages keep this right if the gap, the bleed-margin
     setting, or the device ever changes. */
  .layout { padding: 0; }

  .scene {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .scene__plate {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    image-rendering: pixelated;   /* never smooth the dither */
  }

  /* Both title-bar labels at full black.

     The framework styles .title as primary text and .instance as SECONDARY,
     which is why the date reads dimmer than the message. That is a deliberate
     hierarchy, not a bug — so overriding it needs !important rather than a
     specificity trick: the rule we are beating is
     `.trmnl .screen--4bit .title_bar .instance`, four classes deep.

     On reflective e-ink a secondary grey loses most of its separation from
     the paper, so the date was closer to invisible than to quiet. */
  .title_bar .title,
  .title_bar .instance {
    color: #000 !important;
  }

  /* Breathing room in the title bar.

     The framework computes its padding as

       padding: 0 calc(var(--gap) * var(--framework-layout-title-bar-padding-factor, 1))

     and never assigns that factor — it exists purely as an extension point,
     defaulting to 1, which gives 10px. The bar's corner radius is also 10px,
     so the date began exactly where the curve ended and read as flush.

     Setting the factor rather than overriding padding directly means no
     !important, symmetry on both sides for free, and the value still tracks
     --gap if the bleed-margin setting ever changes. */
  .screen {
    --framework-layout-title-bar-padding-factor: 2;
  }
</style>
